@node CMacs AI Images
@chapter CMacs AI Images: Pictures In

cmacs-ai used to be text in, text out, so no model could look at a
screenshot and ``explain that'' (@pxref{CMacs Deixis Ask}) fell back to
OCR.  ai-glib already had image content (@code{AiImageContent}) and its
providers serialise it; this is the cmacs half: images on every path
that builds a user message (@file{cmacs/ai/cmacs-ai-vision.c}), deciding
whether a model can see them, in-memory captures behind the redaction
rules, image links in a chat, and the @code{images} parameter of
@code{ai_prompt} and @code{ai_call} (@file{lisp/cmacs/cmacs-ai-vision.el}).

@menu
* AI Images Specs::        What an image is, and the checks it passes.
* AI Images Vision::       Whether a model can see it.
* AI Images Capture::      Screen captures, in memory, behind the rules.
* AI Images Chat::         Image links and @kbd{C-c C-i}.
* AI Images Agents::       The @code{images} tool parameter.
* AI Images Options::      Options, and what is not done.
@end menu

@node AI Images Specs
@section An image

An image is a plist, @code{(:file PATH)} or @code{(:data BYTES :mime
TYPE)} with @var{bytes} a unibyte string, and everything that takes
images takes a list of them (one plist alone is a list of one):
@code{cmacs-ai-call}'s @code{:images}; the fifth argument of
@code{cmacs-ai-chat-stream}; the fourth of
@code{cmacs-ai-session-append-message} (user messages only); the seventh
of @code{cmacs-ai--call}; the third of @code{cmacs-ai-harness-send-input};
the sixth of @code{cmacs-ai-textops-stream}.

The C checks each one on the main thread before anything joins a
conversation:

@itemize
@item
@emph{The bytes decide the type.}  PNG, JPEG, GIF and WebP are
recognised by their magic numbers; anything else is refused.  The type
put on the image is always the sniffed one --- exactly
@code{image/png}, @code{image/jpeg}, @code{image/gif} or
@code{image/webp}, the four Claude accepts.  A declared @code{:mime} is
only compared, after dropping parameters and reading @code{image/jpg}
as @code{image/jpeg}; one that disagrees with the bytes is refused.  An
empty image cannot pass.  BMP and SVG are refused, not converted.
@item
@emph{A file is bounded before it is read:} opened
@code{O_NONBLOCK}, a regular file, no larger than
@code{cmacs-ai-image-max-bytes} (10 MB) by its size, and refused if it
grows past that while read.
@item
At most @code{cmacs-ai-image-max-count} (16) per message.
@end itemize

A refusal signals @code{cmacs-ai-error} and leaves the session as it
was.  @code{cmacs-ai-image-parts} runs the checks without sending, and
@code{cmacs-ai-session-message-parts} shows the blocks of a message in a
session.

@node AI Images Vision
@section Can this model see it?

ai-glib has no ``accepts image input'' capability (its
@code{AiImageCapabilities} are about generating images; an
@code{ai_provider_accepts_images (provider, model)} is proposed, not
built).  @code{cmacs-ai-vision-supported-p} decides, first answer wins:

@enumerate
@item
@code{cmacs-ai-vision-model-overrides}, @code{(PROVIDER REGEXP .
BOOLEAN)} on the model name.
@item
@code{cmacs-ai-vision-providers}, @code{(PROVIDER . BOOLEAN)}.
@item
ollama: the model must match @code{cmacs-ai-vision-ollama-models}, a
documented @emph{guess} at the vision families; no model named is a no.
@item
An HTTP provider: @code{cmacs-ai-provider-image-input} builds a request
holding a small marked image through the client's own
@code{build_request} and looks for the image in the JSON --- what the
linked ai-glib really does, cached per client class.  When it cannot
tell, @code{cmacs-ai-vision-http-fallback}.
@item
A CLI provider: @code{cmacs-ai-vision-cli-providers} --- claude-code,
codex-cli, antigravity and acp yes; opencode, claude-tmux, cursor and
grok-build no (they take only a text prompt).
@item
Anything else: no.
@end enumerate

An image is never dropped silently: @code{cmacs-ai-vision-check} refuses
before sending, naming the provider and model, the providers here that
can, and the option that says otherwise.

@node AI Images Capture
@section Capture, in memory, behind the rules

@code{cmacs-ai-capture-region} (a screen region),
@code{cmacs-ai-capture-client} (one window),
@code{cmacs-ai-capture-frame} (this Emacs frame) and
@code{cmacs-ai-capture-clipboard} return @code{(:data PNG :mime
"image/png")}.  Every screen capture is decided as a model would ask,
because it is going to one: a region is refused while an excluded
window is focused or visible in it (the gowl tools' region guard), or
while it covers this Emacs's frame and a frame shows an excluded
buffer; a window when the rules exclude it; a frame when it shows an
excluded buffer.  A failure deciding is a refusal, signalled as
@code{cmacs-ai-capture-refused} with the redaction layer's one fixed
sentence.  A picture is never redacted: all or nothing.

@code{cmacs-ai-png-encode} turns gowl's pixels into PNG bytes in memory
(Cairo, a memory stream), scaled to @code{cmacs-ai-image-max-side}.
Nothing touches the disk unless @code{cmacs-ai-capture-save-directory}
names a directory.

@node AI Images Chat
@section In a chat

Image links in the compose area --- @code{[[file:x.png]]},
@code{[[./x.jpg]]}, @code{[[attachment:x.png]]} --- are sent as images
with the message, in order; the link text stays, so the model and the
transcript can tell them apart.

@kbd{C-c C-i} (@code{cmacs-ai-chat-attach-image}) attaches a file, a
region of the screen (default @code{cmacs-ai-capture-box} around the
pointer), a window, this frame or the clipboard image.  A capture
becomes @code{[[cmacs-image:N][...]]}, a link to bytes the buffer holds
in memory.  It shadows @code{org-ctrl-c-tab} in chat buffers.  A model
that cannot see is refused before anything is captured or sent, and the
compose area is left as it was.

@node AI Images Agents
@section For agents

@code{ai_prompt} and @code{ai_call} take @code{images}, an array of
@code{@{"path": P@}} or @code{@{"data": BASE64, "mime": TYPE@}}.  A path
is held to what @code{project_read_file} reads: inside the workspace
root by true name, not excluded by the redaction rules, a regular file.
Data is bounded before decoding.  A provider that cannot see is a failed
call.  @command{emacsctl tool ai call} passes @code{images} through; the
D-Bus @code{Ai.Call} method (@code{(ssssb)}) forwards to @code{ai_call}
but cannot carry images, and @command{emacsctl ai call} uses it.

@node AI Images Options
@section Options, and what is not done

@table @code
@item cmacs-ai-image-max-bytes
Largest image (10 MB).
@item cmacs-ai-image-max-count
Most images per message (16).
@item cmacs-ai-image-max-side
Captures scaled to this longer side (1568); @code{nil} for full size.
@item cmacs-ai-vision-providers
@itemx cmacs-ai-vision-model-overrides
Your answers, per provider and per model.
@item cmacs-ai-vision-ollama-models
ollama models taken to see.
@item cmacs-ai-vision-cli-providers
@itemx cmacs-ai-vision-http-fallback
@itemx cmacs-ai-vision-cli-programs
The tables behind the decision and the suggestions.
@item cmacs-ai-capture-save-directory
Where captures are also saved; @code{nil} keeps them in memory.
@item cmacs-ai-capture-box
The region offered around the pointer (@code{(900 . 420)}).
@end table

Not done: the harness's Lisp does not attach images yet (its primitive
takes them); a retried or promoted request rebuilt from text carries no
images; no format conversion; frame captures are not scaled.
